  "explicit_limitations": [
    "Multi-agent triage serves strictly as decision support rather than an autonomous oracle: two authors independently audit every NeuG report (91% human-LLM agreement, 87.3% FP recall), and dynamic debugging requires a target debug build capable of attaching a source-level debugger.",
    "19 confirmed bugs on NeuG 0.1.1 under 12-hour saturation campaigns do not establish bug-detection completeness; Section 6 omits a NeuG-specific plan-collapse percentage ablation and omits token/API cost and runtime latency figures for claude-sonnet-4-6.",
    "Evaluation covers four Cypher systems (Neo4j, Memgraph, FalkorDB, NeuG 0.1.1) and does not directly transfer to multi-option GQL or Gremlin/RDF engines; within-system EXPLAIN plan-hash comparison yields a conservative lower bound on collapse (§7 construct validity) and cannot detect defects residing inside a shared compiled plan.",
    "Porting reference methods introduces implementation-induced FPs (up to 59.2% in GraphGenie, Table 3); Section 4.3 FP taxonomy is qualitative over single 12-hour runs rather than multi-seed frequency estimates; and no public GraphWeave repository URL appears in the v1 preprint."
  ],
